  "answer": "**The build and tests now pass.** The second verification run (`20261021T115126Z-3a1d32`) passed build, unit and component. It took one fix cycle.\n\n**What failed:** On the first run the build passed, but the unit stage failed (exit code 2), so component tests never ran. One test failed, `DeltaFormatterTests.Format_FieldInActualNotInExpected_ShowsAbsentSentinel`, once on each target framework (net9.0 and net10.0).\n\n**Root cause:** When a field appears in the actual response but not in the expected one, the failure message labelled the missing side `<not present>`. The test expects `<absent>`, and so do `doc/failure-output.md`, `CHANGELOG.md` and the skill references. The code was wrong, not the test.\n\n**What was changed:** One line in `src/ConfIT/Matching/DeltaFormatter.cs:69` now outputs `<absent>` instead of `<not present>`. No test files were touched.\n\nThe unit stage took about 6.5 minutes on the confirming run, against 2 seconds on the first. That's probably because the first run stopped early, but it's worth knowing if you run it locally. Nothing has been committed.",
